@page "/van-sales/reports/exceptions"
@* Admin and Manager only — see VanSalesActivity.razor. *@
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager")]
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using System.Globalization
@using ShopInventory.Web.Models
@inject IVanSalesReportService VanSalesReportService
@inject IReportExportService ExportService
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>Van Sales Exceptions - Shop Inventory</PageTitle>

@* How the money was settled, and every van document the rest of this suite cannot
   see.

   Carried by wwwroot/css/van-sales.css: the shared `vs-` chrome plus `vsx-` for
   what only this page draws. A prefix nothing else on that sheet owns, because
   sheets here are separated by prefix alone.

   This is not the cash-and-leakage report the plan asked for, and the page says so
   rather than letting a reader assume the comparison was forgotten. Nothing in this
   system records what was banked, so declared-against-banked — the comparison that
   catches theft — cannot be built at all. Declared-against-system is the only
   variance the schema supports and the compliance page already gives it per rep per
   day. For the same reason there is no discount column (neither van ingest path
   writes DiscountPercent, so every van line reads 0.00%) and no returns reason (no
   van endpoint can capture a return).

   What is left is the half nobody asked for. Four things the page has to say out
   loud, because each is a limit on what a figure means rather than a detail of it:

   - The unseen register is read straight from StockReservations rather than through
     VanSalesFactReader, because the reader takes confirmed documents only and by
     construction cannot show these. It must never be read as a second definition of
     a van sale. Expired is the outage signature: a van invoice that could not reach
     SAP is queued, its reservation is left Pending, the cleanup job expires it
     within the hour, and no van report ever counts the money. The suite therefore
     reads lower — which is to say better — exactly on the estate's worst days, and
     this section is the only place that is visible. It leads the page for that
     reason.
   - Held sales must be read against the posting switch, which the report carries as
     Quality.PostingJobEnabled and the page states on the face of the band. "Nothing
     has posted" means something very different when nothing is trying to.
   - The receipt handover is a distribution and never a count of exceptions. Every
     value in it is decided by fields the handset uploads and this repository cannot
     confirm which build the fleet is running, so a one-valued column is an
     unestablished reading rather than good news. NotApplicable in particular was the
     column's default and was never backfilled.
   - Money is a list per currency everywhere it appears, never a scalar, and nothing
     is ever summed across currencies. A figure with no denominator — a rep who took
     nothing, a period that sold nothing — renders as an em dash, never as a zero
     that would read as perfect capture. *@

<div class="vs vsx">

    <div class="vs-head">
        <div>
            <h2 class="vs-title">Exceptions &amp; settlement</h2>
            <p class="vs-subtitle">
                How the fleet was paid over the period, and every van document the rest of these
                reports cannot see — the sales that were made, served and counted nowhere.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="vs-actions">
            <button class="vs-btn" @onclick="ExportAsync" disabled="@(isLoading || report is null)">
                Export
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vs-filters">
        <div class="row g-3">
            @* NocturneDateField and NocturneSelect, never a native date input or select: the
               platform calendar and the platform popup are windows no page stylesheet reaches
               into, and both arrive unreadable on this sheet's dark ground. *@
            <div class="col-md-3">
                <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsx-from">From</label>
                <NocturneDateField Id="vsx-from" @bind-Date="fromDate" AriaLabel="From date" />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-3">
                <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsx-to">To</label>
                <NocturneDateField Id="vsx-to" @bind-Date="toDate" AriaLabel="To date" />
            </div>
            @* The rep filter goes to the server, because it has to reach the unseen and held
               reads as well as the settled ones, and neither of those is on this page to filter
               client-side. The list itself is refilled only on an unfiltered load: narrowing to
               one rep must not empty the picker that got you there. *@
            <div class="col-md-3">
                <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsx-rep">Rep</label>
                <NocturneSelect Id="vsx-rep" Class="nsel-block" TValue="string"
                                Options="RepFilterOptions" @bind-Value="selectedRepId"
                                OnChanged="LoadAsync" AriaLabel="Filter by rep"
                                Placeholder="All reps" />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-3 vs-actions">
                <button class="vs-btn vs-btn-accent" @onclick="LoadAsync" disabled="@isLoading">
                    @(isLoading ? "Loading…" : "Run")
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @if (loadError is not null)
    {
        <div class="vs-notice">@loadError</div>
    }

    @if (isLoading)
    {
        <div class="vs-loading">
            <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" Size="Size.Small" />
            <span>Reading the register…</span>
        </div>
    }
    else if (report is null)
    {
        <div class="vs-empty">
            <div class="vs-empty-title">Nothing loaded yet</div>
            <div>Choose a period and run the report.</div>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        var summary = report.Summary;
        var quality = report.Quality;

        @* The posting switch sits above every held figure it governs, and it is stated whether it
           is on or off. Read only when it is off, a reader who never sees the banner has no way
           to know the state was checked at all. *@
        <div class="vsx-switch @(quality.PostingJobEnabled ? "vsx-switch-on" : "vsx-switch-off")">
            @if (quality.PostingJobEnabled)
            {
                <strong>The van sales posting job is running.</strong>
                <span>
                    An offline sale that is still held is a sale the job has not drained yet, or one
                    it has tried and failed to post. The attempt counts below say which.
                </span>
            }
            else
            {
                <strong>The van sales posting job is switched off in this environment.</strong>
                <span>
                    No offline van sale can reach SAP however long it waits. Every held figure below
                    is the size of a queue, not a posting failure, and it will grow for as long as
                    the switch stays down.
                </span>
            }
        </div>

        <div class="vsx-kpis">
            <div class="vsx-kpi @(summary.UnseenDocumentCount > 0 ? "vsx-kpi-warn" : null)">
                <div class="vsx-kpi-value">@summary.UnseenDocumentCount.ToString("N0")</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-label">Documents unseen</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-sub">@Rate(summary.UnseenRate) of everything captured</div>
            </div>

            <div class="vsx-kpi @(summary.ExpiredDocumentCount > 0 ? "vsx-kpi-warn" : null)">
                <div class="vsx-kpi-value">@summary.ExpiredDocumentCount.ToString("N0")</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-label">Sales lost to an outage</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-sub">expired unconfirmed — made, served, counted nowhere</div>
            </div>

            <div class="vsx-kpi">
                <div class="vsx-kpi-value">@ExposureList(summary.UnseenExposure)</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-label">Money on them</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-sub">absent from every other van report</div>
            </div>

            <div class="vsx-kpi @(summary.HeldSaleCount > 0 ? "vsx-kpi-warn" : null)">
                <div class="vsx-kpi-value">@summary.HeldSaleCount.ToString("N0")</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-label">Held for posting</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-sub">
                    oldest @Count(summary.OldestHeldAgeDays) day(s) · @ExposureList(summary.HeldExposure)
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="vsx-kpi @(summary.SalesWithoutTender > 0 ? "vsx-kpi-warn" : null)">
                <div class="vsx-kpi-value">@Rate(summary.UntenderedRate)</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-label">Settled without a method</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-sub">
                    @summary.SalesWithoutTender.ToString("N0") of @summary.SaleCount.ToString("N0") sales
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="vsx-kpi">
                <div class="vsx-kpi-value">@summary.SaleCount.ToString("N0")</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-label">Sales settled</div>
                <div class="vsx-kpi-sub">
                    @summary.RepCount.ToString("N0") rep(s) · @MoneyList(summary.TotalsByCurrency)
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        @* Always shown. The last caveat is unconditional — declared cash is not compared here —
           so this strip has something to say in every period, including a clean one. *@
        <div class="vsx-caveats">
            <div class="vsx-caveats-head">What this period could not answer</div>
            <ul class="vsx-caveats-list">
                @foreach (var caveat in quality.Caveats)
                {
                    <li>@caveat</li>
                }
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="vsx-sections">
            @foreach (var section in Sections)
            {
                <button type="button"
                        class="vs-chip @(activeSection == section.Key ? "vs-chip-info" : "vs-chip-quiet")"
                        @onclick="() => activeSection = section.Key">
                    @section.Label
                    <span class="vsx-section-count">@section.Count(report)</span>
                </button>
            }
        </div>

        @if (activeSection == SectionUnseen)
        {
            <h3 class="vsx-heading">Documents the rest of the suite cannot see</h3>
            <p class="vsx-note">
                Read straight from the reservations rather than through the shared fact reader,
                which takes confirmed documents only and by construction cannot show these. It is
                not a second definition of a van sale and must never be used as one.
                <strong>Expired is the outage signature.</strong> A van invoice that could not reach
                SAP is queued, its reservation is left pending, and the cleanup job expires it
                within the hour — so the sale was made and the customer served, but no van report
                counts the money. Pending is either an outage in progress or a document written
                moments ago; cancelled and failed are set when a posting attempt failed outright.
            </p>
            @if (report.Unseen.Count == 0)
            {
                <div class="vs-empty">
                    <div class="vs-empty-title">Every van document confirmed</div>
                    <div>
                        No reservation in this period stopped short of confirmation, so nothing was
                        kept out of the other van reports.
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="vs-table-wrap">
                    <table class="vs-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>State</th>
                                <th>Rep</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Documents</th>
                                <th>Money on them</th>
                                <th>First captured</th>
                                <th>Last captured</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var row in report.Unseen)
                            {
                                <tr class="@(row.IsLostSale ? "vsx-lost" : null)">
                                    <td>
                                        @row.Status
                                        @if (row.IsLostSale)
                                        {
                                            <span class="vs-chip vs-chip-bad vsx-inline-chip">lost sale</span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        @row.DisplayName
                                        @if (row.UserId is null)
                                        {
                                            @* Kept rather than dropped: a document nobody owns is
                                               itself the finding. *@
                                            <span class="vs-chip vs-chip-quiet vsx-inline-chip">no rep recorded</span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.DocumentCount.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="@(row.Exposure.Count == 0 ? "vs-metric-none" : null)">
                                        @ExposureList(row.Exposure)
                                    </td>
                                    <td>@Instant(row.EarliestCapturedAt)</td>
                                    <td>@Instant(row.LatestCapturedAt)</td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            }
        }
        else if (activeSection == SectionSettlement)
        {
            <h3 class="vsx-heading">How the money was settled</h3>
            <p class="vsx-note">
                The period's roll-up, which is a different question from the compliance page's split
                per rep-day: a day's split answers whether a rep's cash added up, and a period's
                answers what the fleet is actually being paid in, which is a banking and float
                question. Both classify tender the same way, so the two can never disagree about
                what counts as cash. A sale with no payment method recorded falls in the same bucket
                as a swipe, so it is split onto its own row and marked — one is a banking
                arrangement, the other is a capture failure.
            </p>
            @if (report.Tender.Count == 0)
            {
                <div class="vs-empty">
                    <div class="vs-empty-title">Nothing settled in this period</div>
                    <div>No van sale reached the reporting union between these dates.</div>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="vs-table-wrap">
                    <table class="vs-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Currency</th>
                                <th>Tender</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Documents</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Gross</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Average document</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var row in report.Tender)
                            {
                                <tr class="@(row.Untendered ? "vsx-untendered" : null)">
                                    <td>@row.Currency</td>
                                    <td>
                                        @row.TenderName
                                        @if (row.Untendered)
                                        {
                                            <span class="vs-chip vs-chip-warn vsx-inline-chip">no method recorded</span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.DocumentCount.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.Gross.ToString("N2")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.AverageDocumentValue is null ? "vs-metric-none" : null)">
                                        @Money(row.AverageDocumentValue)
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            }

            <h3 class="vsx-heading">By rep, per currency</h3>
            <p class="vsx-note">
                One row per rep per currency, never a row per rep: the columns are money and money
                is not added across currencies anywhere in this suite. The cash share is what
                decides how much physical money is expected back off a round.
            </p>
            @if (report.TenderByRep.Count == 0)
            {
                <div class="vs-empty">
                    <div class="vs-empty-title">No rep settled anything</div>
                    <div>Nothing in this period reached the reporting union to be split.</div>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="vs-table-wrap">
                    <table class="vs-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Rep</th>
                                <th>Currency</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Documents</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Takings</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Cash</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">EcoCash</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">InnBucks</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Other</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Not recorded</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Cash share</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Untendered</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var row in report.TenderByRep)
                            {
                                <tr>
                                    <td>@row.DisplayName</td>
                                    <td>@row.Currency</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.DocumentCount.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.Gross.ToString("N2")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.CashGross.ToString("N2")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.EcocashGross.ToString("N2")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.InnbucksGross.ToString("N2")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.OtherGross.ToString("N2")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.UntenderedCount > 0 ? "vsx-bad" : null)">
                                        @row.UntenderedGross.ToString("N2")
                                        <span class="vsx-sub">@row.UntenderedCount.ToString("N0") doc(s)</span>
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.CashShare is null ? "vs-metric-none" : null)">
                                        @Rate(row.CashShare)
                                        @if (row.CashShare is { } cash)
                                        {
                                            <span class="vs-meter">
                                                <span class="vs-meter-fill" style="width:@(Meter(cash))%"></span>
                                            </span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.UntenderedShare is null ? "vs-metric-none" : null)">
                                        @Rate(row.UntenderedShare)
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            }
        }
        else if (activeSection == SectionHeld)
        {
            <h3 class="vsx-heading">Offline sales waiting to post</h3>
            <p class="vsx-note">
                An offline van sale is ingested and then held until the posting job drains it. Read
                these against the state of that switch, given above every figure on this page: with
                the job down the queue grows correctly and invisibly, and a rep whose sales have
                never been attempted has done nothing wrong. Nothing here has been established as
                revenue, so its money is never added to a takings figure.
            </p>
            @if (report.Held.Count == 0)
            {
                <div class="vs-empty">
                    <div class="vs-empty-title">Nothing is waiting</div>
                    <div>Every offline van sale captured in this period has reached SAP.</div>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="vs-table-wrap">
                    <table class="vs-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Rep</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Sales</th>
                                <th>Money held</th>
                                <th>Oldest</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Age</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Attempted</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Never attempted</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Failed</th>
                                <th>Last error</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var row in report.Held)
                            {
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        @row.DisplayName
                                        @if (row.UserId is null)
                                        {
                                            <span class="vs-chip vs-chip-quiet vsx-inline-chip">no rep recorded</span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.SaleCount.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="@(row.Exposure.Count == 0 ? "vs-metric-none" : null)">
                                        @ExposureList(row.Exposure)
                                    </td>
                                    <td>@Date(row.OldestDocDate)</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.OldestAgeDays is null ? "vs-metric-none" : null)">
                                        @Count(row.OldestAgeDays)
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.AttemptedCount.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.NeverAttemptedCount == row.SaleCount ? "vsx-quiet-figure" : null)">
                                        @row.NeverAttemptedCount.ToString("N0")
                                        @if (row.NeverAttemptedCount == row.SaleCount && row.SaleCount > 0)
                                        {
                                            @* Nothing has tried to post these. That is a question
                                               about the job, not about the rep. *@
                                            <span class="vs-chip vs-chip-neutral vsx-inline-chip">untouched</span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.FailedCount > 0 ? "vsx-bad" : null)">
                                        @row.FailedCount.ToString("N0")
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vsx-error">
                                        @(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(row.LastError) ? "—" : row.LastError)
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            }
        }
        else if (activeSection == SectionReceipts)
        {
            <h3 class="vsx-heading">The fiscal receipt handover</h3>
            <p class="vsx-note">
                A distribution, and deliberately not a count of exceptions. Every value here is
                decided by fields the handset uploads, and this repository cannot confirm which
                build the fleet is running — so a column reading one value throughout is as likely
                to describe an old handset as a real fiscal problem, and the whole spread is shown
                so a reader can see that for themselves. A row carrying no device signature can
                never be handed to the fiscalisation platform whatever its status says.
                <strong>NotApplicable deserves particular suspicion</strong>: it was the column's
                default when the column was added, nothing backfilled it, and the drain skips it —
                so a sale ingested before the column existed says "nothing to submit" while its
                receipt will in fact never be submitted.
            </p>
            @if (report.ReceiptHandover.Count == 0)
            {
                <div class="vs-empty">
                    <div class="vs-empty-title">No van sales in this period</div>
                    <div>There is no handover distribution to show.</div>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="vs-table-wrap">
                    <table class="vs-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Handover status</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Sales</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">With a signature</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Without one</th>
                                <th>Earliest</th>
                                <th>Latest</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var row in report.ReceiptHandover)
                            {
                                <tr>
                                    <td>
                                        @row.Status
                                        @if (IsUnbackfilled(row.Status))
                                        {
                                            <span class="vs-chip vs-chip-warn vsx-inline-chip">
                                                default, never backfilled
                                            </span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.SaleCount.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.WithSignature.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.WithoutSignature > 0 ? "vsx-bad" : null)">
                                        @row.WithoutSignature.ToString("N0")
                                    </td>
                                    <td>@Date(row.EarliestDocDate)</td>
                                    <td>@Date(row.LatestDocDate)</td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                @if (report.ReceiptHandover.Count <= 1)
                {
                    <p class="vsx-note">
                        Every van sale in this period shares one status, which is what a handset
                        build predating the signed-receipt upload looks like. Read this section as
                        unestablished rather than as good news.
                    </p>
                }
            }
        }
        else if (activeSection == SectionHygiene)
        {
            <h3 class="vsx-heading">What the sales did not carry</h3>
            <p class="vsx-note">
                Every figure here is a capture failure and not a money failure: the sale is real and
                the money is real, and something about it was never written down. A line with a
                quantity and no value is a real zero rather than a rounding artefact — nothing in
                either capture path forbids one, so it is a free issue, a keying slip, or a
                promotion nobody recorded as one. Worst first, because this is a worklist; a clean
                rep is the row nobody needs to read.
            </p>
            @if (report.Hygiene.Count == 0)
            {
                <div class="vs-empty">
                    <div class="vs-empty-title">No rep settled anything</div>
                    <div>There are no captured sales in this period to check.</div>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="vs-table-wrap">
                    <table class="vs-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Rep</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Sales</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">No method</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Untendered</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">No outlet</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Unattributed</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Lines</th>
                                <th class="vs-num">Lines at zero</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var row in report.Hygiene)
                            {
                                <tr class="@(row.IsClean ? "vsx-clean" : null)">
                                    <td>
                                        @row.DisplayName
                                        @if (row.IsClean)
                                        {
                                            <span class="vs-chip vs-chip-clean vsx-inline-chip">nothing outstanding</span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.SaleCount.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.WithoutTender > 0 ? "vsx-bad" : null)">
                                        @row.WithoutTender.ToString("N0")
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.UntenderedRate is null ? "vs-metric-none" : null)">
                                        @Rate(row.UntenderedRate)
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.WithoutOutlet > 0 ? "vsx-bad" : null)">
                                        @row.WithoutOutlet.ToString("N0")
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.UnattributedRate is null ? "vs-metric-none" : null)">
                                        @Rate(row.UnattributedRate)
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="vs-num">@row.LineCount.ToString("N0")</td>
                                    <td class="vs-num @(row.LinesWithoutValue > 0 ? "vsx-bad" : null)">
                                        @row.LinesWithoutValue.ToString("N0")
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            }
        }
    }
</div>

@code {
    private const string SectionUnseen = "unseen";
    private const string SectionSettlement = "settlement";
    private const string SectionHeld = "held";
    private const string SectionReceipts = "receipts";
    private const string SectionHygiene = "hygiene";

    /// <summary>The handover value the column was created with and nothing ever backfilled.</summary>
    private const string UnbackfilledHandoverStatus = "NotApplicable";

    private sealed record Section(string Key, string Label, Func<VanSalesExceptionsReportResponse, string> Count);

    // Unseen leads, ahead of settlement. It is the section that says the rest of the suite is
    // under-reporting, and it is why this page exists.
    private static readonly Section[] Sections =
    [
        new(SectionUnseen, "Unseen", r => r.Summary.UnseenDocumentCount.ToString("N0")),
        new(SectionSettlement, "Settlement", r => r.Tender.Count.ToString("N0")),
        new(SectionHeld, "Held for posting", r => r.Summary.HeldSaleCount.ToString("N0")),
        new(SectionReceipts, "Receipts", r => r.ReceiptHandover.Count.ToString("N0")),
        new(SectionHygiene, "Capture hygiene", r => r.Hygiene.Count.ToString("N0"))
    ];

    private VanSalesExceptionsReportResponse? report;

    private DateTime? fromDate;
    private DateTime? toDate;
    private string? selectedRepId;
    private string activeSection = SectionUnseen;

    private bool isLoading;
    private string? loadError;

    /// <summary>
    /// The reps the period holds, filled from the last unfiltered load.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Built from the report's own rows rather than from the staff list, so the picker cannot offer
    /// somebody with nothing to look at. It is deliberately not refilled while a rep is selected:
    /// the filter goes to the server, so a filtered report contains only the chosen rep and
    /// rebuilding from it would leave a picker of one with no way back to the others.
    /// </remarks>
    private List<RepOption> repOptions = [];

    private sealed record RepOption(Guid Id, string Name, int DocumentCount);

    private IEnumerable<INocturneSelectOption<string>> RepFilterOptions =>
        new[] { NocturneSelectOption.All("All reps") }
            .Concat(repOptions.Select(rep => new NocturneSelectOption<string>(
                rep.Id.ToString("N"),
                rep.Name)
            {
                Hint = rep.DocumentCount.ToString("N0")
            }));

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // CAT, not the server's clock: a trading day belongs to the van.
        var today = DateTime.UtcNow.AddHours(2).Date;
        fromDate = today.AddDays(-13);
        toDate = today;

        await LoadAsync();
    }

    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        isLoading = true;
        loadError = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            var repId = Guid.TryParseExact(selectedRepId, "N", out var parsed)
                ? parsed
                : (Guid?)null;

            report = await VanSalesReportService.GetExceptionsReportAsync(fromDate, toDate, repId);

            if (report is null)
            {
                loadError = "The exceptions report could not be loaded. Check that the API is reachable.";
                return;
            }

            if (repId is null)
            {
                repOptions = RepsIn(report);
            }
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            loadError = $"Failed to load the exceptions report: {ex.Message}";
        }
        finally
        {
            isLoading = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Every rep the period names, counting settled sales, unseen documents and held sales.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The three populations are disjoint by construction — the fact reader takes confirmed and
    /// consolidated documents, the unseen read takes only unconfirmed reservations and the held read
    /// only unconsolidated sales — so the counts add without double-counting anything. The tender
    /// split is left out on purpose: it is one row per rep per currency over the same settled sales
    /// the hygiene rows already count.
    ///
    /// A row with no rep is skipped rather than offered. The API's filter drops unattributed
    /// documents whenever a rep is named, so an "unattributed" entry here would select a report that
    /// cannot contain it.
    /// </remarks>
    private static List<RepOption> RepsIn(VanSalesExceptionsReportResponse report) =>
        report.Hygiene
            .Select(row => new RepOption(row.UserId, row.DisplayName, row.SaleCount))
            .Concat(report.Unseen
                .Where(row => row.UserId is not null)
                .Select(row => new RepOption(row.UserId!.Value, row.DisplayName, row.DocumentCount)))
            .Concat(report.Held
                .Where(row => row.UserId is not null)
                .Select(row => new RepOption(row.UserId!.Value, row.DisplayName, row.SaleCount)))
            .GroupBy(rep => rep.Id)
            .Select(group => new RepOption(
                group.Key,
                group.First().Name,
                group.Sum(rep => rep.DocumentCount)))
            .OrderBy(rep => rep.Name, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
            .ToList();

    private async Task ExportAsync()
    {
        if (report is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            var bytes = ExportService.ExportVanSalesExceptionsToExcel(report);
            var fileName = $"VanSalesExceptions_{DateTime.UtcNow.AddHours(2):yyyyMMdd_HHmmss}.xlsx";

            await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("downloadFile", fileName, Convert.ToBase64String(bytes));
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            loadError = $"The export could not be downloaded: {ex.Message}";
        }
    }

    private static bool IsUnbackfilled(string status) =>
        string.Equals(status, UnbackfilledHandoverStatus, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    // ── Formatting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // An em dash for everything unavailable, and never a zero standing in for one. On this report
    // the distinction carries most of the meaning: a period that sold nothing has no untendered
    // share, a rep who took nothing in a currency has no cash share, and a held sale nobody has
    // dated has no age. A zero in any of those places would read as perfect capture.

    private static string Rate(double? rate) => rate is { } value ? value.ToString("P0") : "—";

    private static string Count(int? count) => count is { } value ? value.ToString("N0") : "—";

    private static string Money(decimal? amount) => amount is { } value ? value.ToString("N2") : "—";

    private static string Date(DateTime? date) => date is { } value ? value.ToString("dd MMM yyyy") : "—";

    /// <summary>
    /// A captured-at instant, shown in CAT. Unlike every date beside it these are UTC moments read
    /// off the reservation rather than trading days, so they are converted before display —
    /// otherwise a document captured late in the evening reads as the previous day's.
    /// </summary>
    private static string Instant(DateTime? instant) =>
        instant is { } value ? value.AddHours(2).ToString("dd MMM HH:mm") : "—";

    /// <summary>Takings, per currency. Never summed across them, on this page or anywhere else.</summary>
    private static string MoneyList(List<VanSalesMoney> totals) =>
        totals.Count == 0
            ? "—"
            : string.Join(", ", totals.Select(total => $"{total.Currency} {total.Gross:N2}"));

    /// <summary>
    /// Money on documents that are not sales. Formatted like takings and typed apart from them,
    /// because nothing in this list has been established as revenue.
    /// </summary>
    private static string ExposureList(List<VanSalesExposure> exposure) =>
        exposure.Count == 0
            ? "—"
            : string.Join(", ", exposure.Select(row => $"{row.Currency} {row.Gross:N2}"));

    private static string Meter(double rate) =>
        Math.Clamp(rate * 100, 0, 100).ToString("F1", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
}
